"/athletes/78360"} "Earl Eby"] " of the United States, who competed in Antwerp, but only in the " [:a {:href "/results/57101"} "800 metres"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} [:a {:href "/athletes/76126"} "Nils Engdahl"] " of Sweden looked good entering the final, as he had won his semi- and quarter-final easily.  Engdahl led early, along with Shea of the U.S., but Rudd took the lead at the head of the straight to win.  Rudd had been born in Devonshire, in the United Kingdom, but was raised in South Africa.  He returned to England to attend Oxford on a Rhodes Scholarship.  He had been a top runner prior to the War, during which he served with the Highland Regiment.  At the 1920 Oxbridge meet, he showed the wide range of his abilities by finishing second in the 100 yards (to " [:a {:href "/athletes/68824"} "Harold Abrahams"] "), tying for first in the 440 yards (with Guy Butler), winning the 880, and finishing fourth in the long jump."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "QF"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "561"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/75317"} "Bevil Rudd"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RSA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RSA.png"}] "RSA"]] [:td {} "51.6 (1 h5)"] [:td {} "51.3est / at 1 metre (2 h4)"] [:td {} "49.7est / chest behind (2 h1)"] [:td {} "49.6 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "382"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/68934"} "Guy Butler"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} "53.2est / at 4 metres (2 h6)"] [:td {} "50.7est